  "title": "Cherokee Syllabary",
  "summary": "Sequoyah, a Cherokee silversmith, devised a writing system with one character per syllable of spoken Cherokee, finished in 1821. Sources give 84 to 86 characters. Its quick adoption allowed the Cherokee Phoenix newspaper to print in the syllabary at New Echota, Georgia, from 1828 to 1834.",
